well today is the start of king week in  the city of las vegas there are lots of  events planned to recognize the great  works of civil rights leader martin  luther king jr bianca holman is live to  tell us more about it sounds like going  to be a lot of good things planned this  week bianca  hey good morning sherry there sure are  so many events planned this weekend next  week to celebrate the life of dr martin  luther king jr and also to know that  it's been 40 years that we've had a  parade to celebrate his life and his  legacy here in las vegas and while there  are lots of things happening to  commemorate his life there's lots of  things happening here in the historic  west side leaders in las vegas want to  ensure black history is preserved the  historic west side legacy parked it  recently opened about a month ago it's  located on mlk in lake mead this honors  36 trailblazers and more will be added  throughout the years this park is just  the beginning of all the work planned  for the area  the landscape of the historic west side  in the next five to ten years will be  completely different to what it is now i  think we have advancements in our  housing  development that are taking place we'll  have more restaurants we'll have other  businesses taking place we're in the  process of taking jackson avenue which  is one of the the original  main streets right in the core of this  request side we're putting a lot of  money into revitalizing that street a  complete street program  and so you just heard from councilman  creer he also spoke about an intense  plan to help re-energize the area that's  where he's from born and raised and  still resides there now and from the  historic west side signs that are there  now the workforce development programs  the beautification grants it's helping  to keep people in the community and  there's also the workforce development  center he tells me that it's going to be  under construction later this year it's  going to be located right next to the  historic west side school so again lots  of things happening in that area in that  neighborhood and of course along with  several events happening at the start of  king week leading up to dr martin luther  king jr day on monday and thereafter  bianca holman live local now
 

